-- title:
--   Theorem 3 — under primal and dual constraint nondegeneracy Algorithm 1 converges with Q-order $1+\tau$
-- statement:
--   Assume the standing assumption of the paper and fix the parameters of Algorithm 1, including $\tau\in(0,1]$ and $\kappa_p,\kappa_c>0$. Let $\{w^k\}=\{(\epsilon^k,X^k,y^k,Z^k)\}$ be an infinite sequence generated by Algorithm 1 and $\bar w=(\bar\epsilon,\bar X,\bar y,\bar Z)$ an accumulation point of it. If primal constraint nondegeneracy holds at $\bar X$ and dual constraint nondegeneracy holds at $(\bar y,\bar Z)$, then the whole sequence converges to $\bar w$, and superlinearly:
--   $$\|w^{k+1}-\bar w\|=O\big(\|w^k-\bar w\|^{1+\tau}\big),$$
--   where $\tau$ controls how accurately the Newton system (24) is solved.
--
--   This is the main result of the paper: superlinear (for $\tau=1$, quadratic) convergence of the Huber-based smoothing Newton method for SDP without strict complementarity.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The norm is the Euclidean norm on $\mathbb R\times\mathbb S^n\times\mathbb R^m\times\mathbb S^n$; $O(\cdot)$ is \"there is $C$ such that for all sufficiently large $k$\".
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: $\mathbb S^n$, $\mathbb R^m$, $\mathbb X=\mathbb S^n\times\mathbb R^m\times\mathbb S^n$ with the trace inner product and Euclidean norms → `SymMat (Fin n)` (Frobenius inner product = trace inner product), `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)`, `WithLp 2` products; reason: Lean convention; the same spaces, inner products and norms
--   - encoding: the standing assumption of p.2 (an optimal solution of (1) exists and Slater's condition holds), stated once for the whole paper → the explicit hypothesis `D.Standing`; reason: the paper assumes it throughout ("In this paper, we assume", p.2)
--   - encoding: "the infinite sequence generated by Algorithm 1" → any `w` with `IsRun D θ x0 w`: $w^0=(\hat\epsilon,x^0)$, and each step uses some direction satisfying $\Delta\epsilon=-\epsilon+\zeta\hat\epsilon$ and (25) and the smallest Armijo exponent; $\hat{\mathcal E}(w^k)\neq0$ for all $k$; reason: Algorithm 1 lets any direction meeting (25) be chosen; the statement covers every such choice
--   - encoding: dual constraint nondegeneracy "at $(\bar y,\bar Z)$" → `DualNondeg D Z̄`, a condition on $\bar Z$ alone; reason: condition (10) involves only $\bar Z$; $\bar y$ is the dual variable of the same KKT point
--   - reading: (10): "a feasible solution $(\bar y,\bar Z)\in\mathbb R^n\times\mathbb S^n_+$" → $\bar y\in\mathbb R^m$; reason: $y$ is the dual variable of the $m$ constraints of (2); $\mathbb R^n$ is a misprint
--   - encoding: "accumulation point" → `MapClusterPt w̄ atTop w`; reason: the standard cluster-point notion for sequences
--   - encoding: $O(\|w^k-\bar w\|^{1+\tau})$ → $\exists C,\ \forall^{\mathrm f} k,\ \|w^{k+1}-\bar w\|\le C\|w^k-\bar w\|^{1+\tau}$ (real power), $C$ after the run and $\bar w$; reason: the definition of $O$ as $k\to\infty$
-- source:
--   Liang, Sun & Toh, A Squared Smoothing Newton Method for Semidefinite Programming, arXiv:2303.05825v4, Theorem 3, p.15 (proof: Appendix K)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HuberSNSDP_Algorithm

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace Topology
open Filter SunNLSDP.Equiv NonsmoothNewton.Shared

namespace HuberSNSDP

/-- Theorem 3, p.15 (Liang, Sun & Toh, arXiv:2303.05825v4).

Let `(ε̄, X̄, ȳ, Z̄)` be an accumulation point of the infinite sequence `{(εᵏ, Xᵏ, yᵏ, Zᵏ)}` generated by
Algorithm 1. Suppose that the primal constraint nondegeneracy condition holds at `X̄`, and the dual
constraint nondegeneracy condition holds at `(ȳ, Z̄)`. Then the whole sequence converges to
`(ε̄, X̄, ȳ, Z̄)` superlinearly:
`‖(εᵏ⁺¹ − ε̄, Xᵏ⁺¹ − X̄, yᵏ⁺¹ − ȳ, Zᵏ⁺¹ − Z̄)‖ = O(‖(εᵏ − ε̄, Xᵏ − X̄, yᵏ − ȳ, Zᵏ − Z̄)‖^{1+τ})`,
with `τ ∈ (0, 1]` the parameter of Algorithm 1.

**Formalization Note.** The run is any infinite sequence of Algorithm 1 (`IsRun`: every admissible
inexact direction (25), the smallest Armijo exponent); "accumulation point" is `MapClusterPt`;
`O(·)` is `∃ C, ∀ᶠ k`; the norm is the Euclidean norm on `ℝ × Sⁿ × ℝᵐ × Sⁿ`; the standing
assumption of p.2 is a hypothesis. -/
theorem theorem_3 {n m : ℕ} (D : SDPData n m) (hD : D.Standing) (θ : Params) (x0 : XSpace n m)
    (w : ℕ → ISpace n m) (hw : IsRun D θ x0 w) (wbar : ISpace n m)
    (hacc : MapClusterPt wbar atTop w) (hP : D.PrimalNondeg (XOf wbar))
    (hDu : D.DualNondeg (ZOf wbar)) :
    Tendsto w atTop (𝓝 wbar) ∧
      ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ᶠ k in atTop, ‖w (k + 1) - wbar‖ ≤ C * ‖w k - wbar‖ ^ (1 + θ.tau) := by sorry

end HuberSNSDP
